Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&nbsp;

 Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.

 Purpose

 We are seeking an exceptional, results-driven&nbsp; Senior Manager of Additive Manufacturing Operations &nbsp;to lead and scale our Factory 1 production organization. This is a&nbsp;high-impact leadership role responsible for driving world-class execution across safety, quality, delivery, cost, and people development while shaping the future of manufacturing. &nbsp; 

 The Additive Manufacturing organization leverages proprietary, state-of-the-art systems and processes to execute metal laser powder bed fusion (LPBF),&nbsp;depowdering, manual and automated support removal, surface finishing, heat treatment, and inspection across multiple factory sites supporting both prototype and high-rate production. &nbsp; 

 This role is ideal for an ambitious operations leader who thrives in fast-paced, high-growth environments and combines strong manufacturing fundamentals with data-driven decision making, automation, and continuous improvement. Beyond delivering daily operational performance, this leader will develop people, build scalable operating systems, and partner with engineering to industrialize new technologies that will define the next generation of manufacturing. &nbsp; 

 The ideal candidate is energized by difficult manufacturing challenges, inspires high-performing teams, and is passionate about building organizations capable of delivering exceptional results. &nbsp; 

 The Role

 Operational Leadership &nbsp; 


 Lead Factory 1 additive manufacturing operations to achieve world-class performance in safety, quality, delivery, cost, and equipment reliability.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Build, develop, and mentor a high-performing team while fostering a culture of accountability, ownership, urgency, and continuous improvement.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Drive disciplined daily management through standard work, visual management, structured problem solving, and operational rigor.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Optimize&nbsp;manufacturing flow by increasing equipment uptime,&nbsp;eliminating&nbsp;bottlenecks, improving process repeatability, and maximizing production throughput.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Partner closely with Platform Development, Manufacturing Engineering, and Automation teams to successfully launch new equipment, technologies, and manufacturing capabilities.&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Operational Excellence &nbsp; 


 Champion Lean Manufacturing principles and continuous&nbsp;improvement across all additive manufacturing processes.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Establish scalable operating systems that improve efficiency, stability, and manufacturing readiness as production grows.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Utilize manufacturing data, KPIs, and analytics to drive operational decisions and prioritize improvement initiatives.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Develop meaningful performance dashboards and operating rhythms that enable rapid identification and resolution of production issues.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Lead initiatives to improve Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE), first-pass yield, cycle time, labor productivity, and cost per part.&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Equipment Reliability &amp; Technical Capability &nbsp; 


 Continue developing the in-house Additive Manufacturing Service organization by strengthening technical capability, preventive maintenance programs, troubleshooting processes, and technician training.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Drive reliability initiatives that maximize printer availability, reduce unplanned downtime, and improve long-term equipment performance.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Partner with technical teams to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;recurring equipment issues and implement sustainable corrective actions.&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Performance Monitoring &amp; Compliance &nbsp; 


 Ensure strict adherence to Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES), work instructions, process controls, and quality standards.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Monitor key operational metrics and hold teams accountable for achieving business&nbsp;objectives.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Drive disciplined root cause analysis and corrective actions to&nbsp;eliminate&nbsp;recurring manufacturing issues.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Develop clear, actionable operational reporting that enables data-driven decision making across the organization.&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Safety, Quality &amp; Financial Management &nbsp; 


 Foster a safety-first culture aligned with Environmental Health &amp; Safety (EHS) standards and best practices.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Partner with EHS to proactively develop and implement safety initiatives that reduce operational risk.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Ensure manufacturing processes consistently meet internal quality requirements and applicable industry standards.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Develop, manage, and execute the Factory 1 Additive Manufacturing operating budget while balancing&nbsp;productivity, cost, and long-term capability investments. 


 Basic Qualifications


 Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls.&nbsp;



 Demonstrated success leading complex manufacturing operations in high-performance production environments.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Proven ability to build, develop, and lead high-performing technical organizations.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Strong understanding of Lean Manufacturing, operational excellence, and continuous improvement methodologies.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience using&nbsp;manufacturing data and operational metrics to drive strategic decision making and measurable business results.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Proven ability to execute in startup or rapidly scaling manufacturing environments while effectively navigating ambiguity and change.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Demonstrated success improving operational performance through equipment reliability, process optimization, and organizational development.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Bachelor's or&nbsp;Master's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Weld Engineering, or a related technical discipline (or equivalent practical experience).&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Preferred Qualifications


 Leadership experience in metal additive manufacturing or other advanced manufacturing environments.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience with Laser Powder Bed Fusion (LPBF) production systems.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience with aerospace manufacturing standards, including AS9100 and NADCAP.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience implementing Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, Theory of Constraints, or similar operational excellence methodologies.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience leading automation, Industry 4.0, MES, or digital manufacturing initiatives.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Demonstrated success scaling manufacturing organizations through periods of rapid growth.&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 &nbsp;
 Pay Range
 $156,640 &mdash; $215,380 USD 


 What We Offer Our Regular, Full-Time Employees: 


 Holistic Compensation Package: Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you're truly valued for your contributions.

 Wellness and Time Off: Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.

 Comprehensive Health and Wellness: Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.

 Investment in Growth: We're committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.

 Collaborative and High-Performing Environment: Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we're disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&nbsp;



 Equal Employment Opportunity 
 Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act. 
 EEO Poster&nbsp; 

 In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&nbsp; 
 &nbsp; 
 E-Verify: Right to Work 
 Our company participates in E-Verify . E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees. 
 Eligibility to Work Poster (English) |&nbsp; Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish) 
 &nbsp; 
 Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO) 
 Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. 

 No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.

Material Bank is the world’s largest material marketplace for the architecture and design industry. Operating in 37 countries, our platform has become the standard for design professionals around the globe. Every day, Material Bank connects thousands of designers with tens of thousands of materials from leading brands. Material Bank is the fastest and most powerful way for design professionals to search, sample, and specify materials.

 P osition Summary &nbsp; 

 Material Bank is seeking a Director of Operations to lead our highly automated Olive Branch distribution center. This leader is accountable for end-to-end fulfillment across multiple business lines and a shared inventory of hundreds of thousands of SKUs, including inbound, inventory, picking, packing, shipping, transportation, labor, quality, safety, automation, and supporting systems. The role combines hands-on floor leadership, data-driven decision making, strategic technology initiatives, and development of a strong management team. &nbsp; 

 What You'll Do 

 Operations &amp; Service Delivery &nbsp; 


 Lead multi-shift receiving, put-away, replenishment, picking, pre-pack, custom packing, shipping, and returns, ensuring daily order cutoffs and service commitments are met. &nbsp; 

 Oversee fulfillment for member sampling, e-commerce, and third-party logistics (3PL) clients from a shared inventory pool; establish capacity and contingency plans for promotions and peak periods. &nbsp; 

 Lead operational onboarding of Brand Partners and 3PL clients; contribute process design, cost and labor models, launch readiness, and operational inputs to RFPs. &nbsp; 

 Act as a senior operational contact for key partners and clients, resolving service issues and maintaining SLAs. &nbsp; 

 Represent Operations in facility projects, process changes, inventory moves, and new program launches, ensuring operational readiness and minimal disruption. &nbsp; 


 Inventory, Transportation &amp; Financial Performance &nbsp; 


 Own inbound execution, inventory accuracy, cycle counting, discrepancy resolution, location integrity, and coordination of inbound scheduling, ASNs, and replenishment. &nbsp; 

 Oversee parcel and freight performance, carrier relationships, transportation costs, surcharges, billing accuracy, and cross-border shipping requirements. &nbsp; 

 Own operating budgets, margin targets, cost per unit, labor productivity, and staffing plans by process and shift; manage staffing partner relationships. &nbsp; 

 Prioritize and deliver process and labor improvements with measurable, recurring savings. &nbsp; 


 Automation, Systems &amp; Continuous Improvement &nbsp; 


 Lead operational use of robotics and automation, including AMRs, and evaluate emerging solutions such as goods-to-person systems. &nbsp; 

 Own operational requirements for WMS and related WES/WCS systems; partner on vendor evaluations, capital business cases, ROI analysis, pilots, and rollouts, holding technology and automation partners accountable for performance. &nbsp; 

 Drive standard work, SOP compliance, process mapping, root-cause analysis, and quality standards across fulfillment processes, packaging, inventory handling, and facility conditions. &nbsp; 

 Maintain a strong safety culture and compliance with OSHA and applicable requirements. &nbsp; 


 Leadership, Data &amp; Culture &nbsp; 


 Lead, recruit, coach, and develop Operations Managers, Supervisors, Team Leads, and hourly associates across shifts, building leadership depth, engagement, and retention. &nbsp; 

 Establish daily operating rhythms and KPI dashboards covering service, quality, cost, productivity, and safety; use data to drive timely decisions. &nbsp; 

 Promote practical adoption of AI and technology for reporting, analysis, documentation, and operational decision making. &nbsp; 

 Build succession depth and a culture of ownership, accountability, respect, and continuous improvement. &nbsp; 


 What You'll Bring 

 Required &nbsp; 


 10+ years of experience in distribution, fulfillment, supply chain, or a related field, including 7+ years managing teams, managers, and multi-shift operations. &nbsp; 

 Experience owning operating budgets, cost-per-unit or labor productivity metrics, and high-volume WMS-enabled operations with robotics or automation. &nbsp; 

 Experience managing parcel and freight operations and carrier relationships. &nbsp; 

 Strong analytical capability, advanced Excel skills, and familiarity with BI/reporting tools; openness to AI and emerging technologies. &nbsp; 

 Strong leadership, attention to detail, proactive problem solving, and ability to manage competing priorities in time-sensitive environments. &nbsp; 

 Availability to work nonstandard hours, including peak periods; ability to lift up to 25 pounds regularly. &nbsp; 


 Preferred &nbsp; 


 Bachelor's degree in Supply Chain , Operations, Engineering, Business, or a related field; MBA a plus . &nbsp; 

 Experience in multi-client 3PL, e-commerce, or small-parcel /sample fulfillment. &nbsp; 

 Experience with WMS or automation implementations, vendor RFPs, and capital investment cases. &nbsp; 

 Knowledge of international shipping and customs, especially Canada and the UK. &nbsp; 

 Experience managing staffing agencies or labor partners. &nbsp; 

 Lean, Six Sigma, or related continuous improvement training or certification. &nbsp; 


 What you’ll get from us: 


 Our people : We are a growth-driven team that values efficiency, builds smart automation, operates in small empowered teams, and moves quickly from idea to execution. 

 Relaxation and Celebrations : Flexible PTO, Sick Days, Paid National Holidays, and even more (ask us about this when we connect).&nbsp; 

 Health Benefits : &nbsp;We&nbsp; contribute &nbsp;to your medical, dental, vision and short-term/long-term&nbsp; disability plans&nbsp; and have a strong employee assistance program.&nbsp; 

 Plan for your Retirement : &nbsp;401(k)&nbsp; eligible &nbsp;after your first 90 day's employed! 

 Giving Back : We sponsor multiple events throughout the year to help out our communities.&nbsp; 

 Growth : We’ll help you take your career to the next level. We want you to be creative and take initiative which will allow you to grow and create within the company. Most importantly, be the best at what matters!&nbsp; 

 Flexible Work Schedules : With business units and employees across the globe, Material Technologies has embraced a  hybrid  working  model allowing department leaders to decide on the best approach for their respective teams, whether that be remote, in person, or a little of both.&nbsp;&nbsp; 


 Material Bank is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity, and all applicants will be considered for employment without attention to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, national origin, veteran or disability status or other status protected under any applicable federal, state or local law.

