&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:contact@anduril.com&quot;&gt;contact@anduril.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Axon and be a Force for Good.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of Mission Engineers who serve as Axon’s embedded builders and operational partners inside strategic public safety agencies. Mission Engineers work face-to-face with the people doing the work, diagnose how the agency operates, and build the workflows, automations, integrations, and AI-enabled solutions that measurably improve it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Manager, you will create the environment in which that work succeeds. You will coach experienced individual contributors, set a clear bar for technical delivery and agency partnership, and help the team turn ambiguous field problems into secure, maintainable solutions that reach production and earn sustained adoption. You will stay close enough to the portfolio to recognize patterns, anticipate risk, and connect what the team learns in the field back to Product, Engineering, and the broader organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success is reflected in agencies becoming more capable, Mission Engineers growing into trusted transformation leaders, and strong field solutions becoming reusable patterns that benefit customers beyond a single engagement. Axon’s mission is to Protect Life, and this team is one of the most direct ways we advance that mission alongside the agencies we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Southeast US Regionally based with Travel up to 40%&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: &lt;/strong&gt;Senior Director, Customer Deployment &amp;amp; Mission Engineering&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Individual Contributors&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Lead, Coach, and Develop Mission Engineers&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a distributed team of embedded Mission Engineers working across strategic agency environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach individual contributors through complex technical decisions, ambiguous customer problems, executive conversations, and high-stakes delivery moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear expectations for ownership, technical quality, onsite partnership, production delivery, adoption, documentation, and measurable agency impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build individualized development plans and create opportunities for Mission Engineers to expand their technical range, executive presence, and transformation leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of curiosity, candor, responsible experimentation, continuous learning, and shared accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support thoughtful team growth by selecting and onboarding people who can both build practical solutions and earn credibility with agency stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Set the Bar for Agency Outcomes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Mission Engineers begin with the agency’s mission, operational workflow, and desired outcome before selecting or building a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Require clear baselines, success criteria, and adoption measures so impact is demonstrated rather than assumed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the team from discovery through production use, iteration, handoff, and sustained adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help Mission Engineers balance immediate agency needs with secure, maintainable, and scalable solution design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce that success means the agency is more capable—not that one individual has become indispensable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Own a Strategic Mission Engineering Portfolio&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain visibility across strategic agencies, active builds, adoption progress, technical risk, and emerging operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match Mission Engineer capability and level to agency complexity, transformation opportunity, and stakeholder environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use operating reviews and portfolio data to identify delivery risks, recurring friction, adoption barriers, and opportunities for reuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step into critical situations with structure and calm while coaching the accountable Mission Engineer to remain in ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive consistent execution across embedded engagements without forcing every agency problem into the same playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Advance Technical and AI-Enabled Delivery&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain sufficient fluency across SaaS, cloud services, APIs, enterprise integrations, hardware, data, and modern AI tooling to coach technical decisions and challenge weak reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team decide when to configure the platform, when to extend it, and when a net-new build is justified&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish expectations for validation, observability, fallback paths, maintainability, documentation, and responsible use of sensitive data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure solutions uphold CJIS requirements, evidence integrity, privacy, approved-tooling standards, and other applicable security controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage practical use of AI to accelerate work while preserving human ownership of architecture, accuracy, and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Turn Field Learning Into Organizational Leverage&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build mechanisms for Mission Engineers to document and share reusable workflows, integrations, frameworks, and playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns across agencies and help convert successful one-off solutions into repeatable capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create strong feedback loops with Product and Engineering around recurring workflow friction, unmet operational needs, and product opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Mission Operators, Customer Success, Deployment, Professional Services, Support, Sales, Product, Engineering, and Enablement so agencies experience coordinated execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share portfolio insights with senior leaders to influence investment, prioritization, staffing, and the evolution of the Mission Engineering operating model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Lead Executive and Agency Engagement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with command staff, agency executives, technical leaders, and internal senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior partner during agency-impacting incidents, high-visibility deployments, and moments that require clear trade-offs or executive alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical and operational issues into decisions that are clear to both technical teams and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach Mission Engineers to challenge requests constructively, communicate candidly, and leave stakeholders with a practical path forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Required&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in customer-facing technical delivery, systems integration, solutions engineering, implementation consulting, operational transformation, or comparable environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading and developing senior technical individual contributors in customer-facing organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success coaching teams that deliver secure, production-ready solutions in complex customer environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading distributed or field-based teams across multiple customers, regions, or engagement models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of improving technical execution, adoption, operational outcomes, and delivery consistency across a portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad technical fluency across SaaS platforms, cloud services, APIs, networking, hardware, integrations, data workflows, and AI-enabled technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence with the ability to earn trust, communicate trade-offs, and guide decisions with command staff and senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinking and the ability to distinguish isolated issues from patterns that require a scalable solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-informed leadership approach using baselines, production delivery, adoption, operational improvement, quality, and reuse to evaluate performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort leading through ambiguity while creating clarity around ownership, priorities, and success criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain CJIS compliance and exercise sound judgment with highly sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in public safety, law enforcement, defense, government technology, or another mission-critical operating environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CAD, RMS, digital evidence, real-time operations, or integrated public safety ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams that build automations, integrations, operational workflows, internal tools, or AI-enabled solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience converting field-developed solutions into reusable frameworks, product improvements, or organizational playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with technical talent development, competency frameworks, or academy-style enablement programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Additional Information&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We recognize that leaders may arrive through different paths. If you have developed technically curious customer-facing teams, helped people turn ambiguous operational problems into working solutions, and care deeply about measurable customer impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits that Benefit You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and 401k with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave for all&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, Vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fitness Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emotional &amp;amp; Mental Wellness support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And yes, we have snacks in our offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits listed herein may vary depending on the nature of your employment and the location where you work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement? That&#39;s ok. At Axon, we Aim Far. We think big with a long-term view because we want to reinvent the world to be a safer, better place. We are also committed to building diverse teams that reflect the communities we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they check every box in the job description. If you’re excited about this role and our mission to Protect Life but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification listed here, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above job description is not intended as, nor should it be construed as, exhaustive of all duties, responsibilities, skills, efforts, or working conditions associated with this job. The job description may change or be supplemented at any time in accordance with business needs and conditions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Some roles may also require legal eligibility to work in a firearms environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We collect personal information from applicants to evaluate candidates for employment. You may request access, deletion, or exercise other CCPA rights at&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;mailto:axongreenhousesupport@axon.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;mailto:axongreenhousesupport@axon.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;axongreenhousesupport@axon.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;or via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://privacyportal.onetrust.com/webform/0efc1702-9321-4119-bc9d-a06c3a1d3e4e/ca57cc26-a159-4193-9f6e-58ffe3fd2509&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://privacyportal.onetrust.com/webform/0efc1702-9321-4119-bc9d-a06c3a1d3e4e/ca57cc26-a159-4193-9f6e-58ffe3fd2509&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Axon Privacy Web Form&lt;/a&gt;. For more information, please see the Your California Privacy Rights section of our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.axon.com/candidateprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.axon.com/candidateprivacypolicy&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Axon’s mission is to Protect Life and is committed to the well-being and safety of its employees as well as Axon’s impact on the environment. All Axon employees must be aware of and committed to the appropriate environmental, health, and safety regulations, policies, and procedures. Axon employees are empowered to report safety concerns as they arise and activities potentially impacting the environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer that promotes justice, advances equity, values diversity and fosters inclusion. We’re committed to hiring the best talent — regardless of race, creed, color, ancestry, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship status, marital status, disability, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances — and empowering all of our employees so they can do their best work. If you have a disability or special need that requires assistance or accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please email &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitingops@axon.com&quot;&gt;recruitingops@axon.com. &lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;Please note that this email address is for accommodation purposes only. Axon will not respond to inquiries for other purposes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Phishing alert:&amp;nbsp; Axon will never ask you to pay for any part of the hiring process, including training, equipment, or background checks. We do not make job offers via text message, WhatsApp, or instant messaging platforms without a formal interview process.&amp;nbsp; All legitimate job openings are listed on our official careers page at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.axon.com/careers&quot;&gt;https://www.axon.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;If you receive a suspicious offer or outreach from an email address that is not &lt;strong&gt;@axon.com&lt;/strong&gt;, or if you are asked for sensitive personal information (bank details, Social Security Number) prematurely, please ignore the message and report it to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitingops@axon.com&quot;&gt;recruitingops@axon.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Formlabs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you want to change how the world creates?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Formlabs, we’re building the tools that make it possible for anyone to bring their ideas to life, from cutting-edge products to life-saving medical devices. Our 3D printing technology powers innovation at more than 50,000 industry leaders worldwide, including Apple, Google, Tesla, New Balance, and NASA. Together, we’re helping everyone design, prototype, and manufacture faster than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of hands-on builders, engineers, and innovators reinventing how the world makes physical things. If you’re ready to shape the future of fabrication, come build it with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Formlabs is manufacturing thousands of printers, an enormous task – and the complexity will grow as we build tens and even hundreds of thousands of electronic products each year. We are looking for someone who will lead the process to take newly innovated products to mass production.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you are a seasoned manufacturing leader who has brought new products to market, we want you to join our team as our &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Head of Manufacturing Engineering.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage a direct team of 15+ manufacturing engineers, manufacturing software engineers and program managers responsible for developing and maintaining the manufacturing tools, systems and processes that bring Formlabs products to the market&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead the operationalizing of our products through strong program management processes that define and execute requirements from both design and operations teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop strong processes and NPI accountability crossfades to bring great products to the market via leadership in DFM, DTC &amp;amp; DFQ areas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Aggressive cost management to facilitate speed to market and then market leading cost structures of components and finished products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take design intent manufacturing tools/processes and operationalize those for high volume, consistent quality and low cost manufacturing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Integrate process discipline, hardware fixtures, software calibration routines and strong management tools to launch and optimize production processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead and enable Formlabs and 3rd party manufacturing sites globally&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Expand the manufacturing capabilities of our global supply chain to include new vertically integrated functions as well as additional outsourced capabilities, including ODM, JDM, white labeled) to meet the growing product requirements of Formlabs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Forward thinking strategy of how to ensure Formlabs manufacturing continues to be a strategic advantage and industry disrupter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build people, processes and technology to enable Formlabs continued business growth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A leader who can hire, manage and develop a team of diverse supply chain, manufacturing and engineering professionals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Highly technical manufacturing/operations leader&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;NPI experience bringing new electro-mechanical products to market&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience managing leveraging partnerships in Asia to bring products to market&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Have built organizations and processes for high growth companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with budget and business plan development&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A driving change agent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust equity program to build future wealth through RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive healthcare coverage (Medical, Dental, Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K matching and access to financial advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid Parental Leave (up to 16 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tenure-based paid Sabbatical Leave (up to 6 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Out of Office Plan – Take time when you need it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ample on-site parking &amp;amp; pre-tax commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthy on-site lunches, snacks, beverages, &amp;amp; treats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular sponsored professional development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many opt-in culture events across our diverse community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And of course… unlimited 3D prints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company.&amp;nbsp; We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Even if you don&#39;t check every box, but see yourself contributing, please apply.&lt;/strong&gt; Help us build an inclusive community that will change the face of 3D printing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equity is a big part of the compensation package at Formlabs - every employee receives equity because everyone contributes to building the company. We have a lot of confidence in the products we’re building and the impact we’re making, and you should too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is the other part of our compensation package, and it is carefully determined based on your skills, experience, and expected impact. Equity and base pay combine to make up your total compensation package at Formlabs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base pay range for this role is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Formlabs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you want to change how the world creates?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Formlabs, we’re building the tools that make it possible for anyone to bring their ideas to life, from cutting-edge products to life-saving medical devices. Our 3D printing technology powers innovation at more than 50,000 industry leaders worldwide, including Apple, Google, Tesla, New Balance, and NASA. Together, we’re helping everyone design, prototype, and manufacture faster than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of hands-on builders, engineers, and innovators reinventing how the world makes physical things. If you’re ready to shape the future of fabrication, come build it with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;VP of Operations&lt;/strong&gt; to join our leadership team and contribute to the global strategy and execution of operations at Formlabs. This executive will lead manufacturing engineering, supply demand management, logistics, supply chain, or materials operations—ensuring precision, scale, and efficiency across our entire product ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our business expands across hardware, software, and materials, this leader will define how we evolve our operational processes, expand our global reach, and unlock new opportunities for growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report directly to the Chief Operating Officer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a multi-year strategy to scale Formlabs’ global operations and expand product capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead manufacturing and operations engineering, developing and refining processes and tooling that ensure high-quality, high-precision products at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee supply demand management: forecasting demand, aligning supply to financial and sales goals, managing factory builds, and ensuring smooth customer allocation during NPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive logistics and supply chain excellence: negotiating with partners, optimizing global systems and processes, and delivering a seamless customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand our global manufacturing footprint and partnerships to meet increasing demand across hardware and materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with R&amp;amp;D, product, and go-to-market teams to support new product introductions and material launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and pursue adjacent business opportunities that drive revenue growth and margin expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best-in-class operational practices, cost structures, and sustainability measures to strengthen market leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or equivalent leadership experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in operations, supply chain, and manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success scaling global, multi-site manufacturing networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise leading operations across manufacturing engineering, supply chain and or logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building strong vendor relationships and negotiating high-value contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to craft and execute long-term strategies that expand capabilities, improve margins, and enable growth at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust equity program to build future wealth through RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive healthcare coverage (Medical, Dental, Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K matching and access to financial advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid Parental Leave (up to 16 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tenure-based paid Sabbatical Leave (up to 6 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Out of Office Plan – Take time when you need it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ample on-site parking &amp;amp; pre-tax commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthy on-site lunches, snacks, beverages, &amp;amp; treats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular sponsored professional development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many opt-in culture events across our diverse community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And of course… unlimited 3D prints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company.&amp;nbsp; We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Even if you don&#39;t check every box, but see yourself contributing, please apply.&lt;/strong&gt; Help us build an inclusive community that will change the face of 3D printing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equity is a big part of the compensation package at Formlabs - every employee receives equity because everyone contributes to building the company. We have a lot of confidence in the products we’re building and the impact we’re making, and you should too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is the other part of our compensation package, and it is carefully determined based on your skills, experience, and expected impact. Equity and base pay combine to make up your total compensation package at Formlabs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base pay range for this role is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operations Director is responsible for leading and coordinating key operational functions of the manufacturing facility, including &lt;strong&gt;Production Planning, Supply Chain, Environmental Health &amp;amp; Safety (EHS), and Infrastructure/Construction Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position plays a critical role in ensuring production readiness, material availability, operational continuity, regulatory compliance, facility development, and cross-functional execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operations Director will work closely with Manufacturing, Quality, Engineering, Finance, Human Resources, and other functional leaders to support safe, efficient, and scalable operations of the Chicago manufacturing facility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Production Planning &amp;amp; Operations Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead production planning and scheduling based on demand, capacity, materials, and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage short- and long-term production plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate manpower, equipment, and materials to achieve production targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor plan execution and identify delivery risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional efforts to resolve production and operational constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track key KPIs, including production attainment, inventory, material availability, delivery, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support S&amp;amp;OP and capacity planning processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Supply Chain Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead plant supply chain operations, including production planning, materials, procurement, inventory, warehousing, and logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure material availability while maintaining optimal inventory levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve inventory turnover and reduce excess and obsolete stock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier performance and supply continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify supply chain risks and implement contingency plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage domestic and international logistics activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead continuous improvement in cost, efficiency, and delivery performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Environmental, Health &amp;amp; Safety (EHS)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the plant’s EHS programs and team to ensure compliance with safety and environmental regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a strong safety culture and drive workplace safety initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee inspections, risk assessments, corrective actions, and emergency preparedness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor EHS performance and implement corrective actions as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams to improve safety and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory audits, inspections, and permitting activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Infrastructure &amp;amp; Construction Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead facility engineering, infrastructure, and construction projects supporting plant operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee plant expansion, renovations, and infrastructure improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contractors, vendors, and project stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure projects meet scope, budget, schedule, quality, and safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain critical facility systems, utilities, and infrastructure readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production line installation, commissioning, and facility startup activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage operational processes across planning, supply chain, EHS, and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead operational reviews and drive action item completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate operational risks to plant leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement continuous improvement initiatives focused on safety, cost, delivery, inventory, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive KPI-based decision-making and operational visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ERP/MRP and digitalization initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster collaboration across Operations, Manufacturing, Quality, Engineering, Finance, HR, and IT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and mentor managers and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish organizational structure, goals, and succession plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and retain key talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive performance, accountability, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative, safety-focused, high-performance culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Supply Chain Management, Engineering, Operations Management, Business Administration, or a related field required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree or MBA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years of progressive experience&lt;/strong&gt; in manufacturing operations, supply chain, production planning, engineering, or related functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of leadership experience&lt;/strong&gt; managing managers and/or multiple operational functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in large-scale manufacturing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in production planning, supply chain management, and plant operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of EHS management and U.S. regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting facility construction, plant expansion, infrastructure, or manufacturing engineering projects strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of ERP/MRP systems; SAP experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in &lt;strong&gt;lithium-ion battery, EV, automotive, energy storage, electronics, or advanced manufacturing&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting the launch or ramp-up of a new manufacturing facility in the United States.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex global supply chains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with high-volume automated manufacturing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with international and cross-cultural teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, S&amp;amp;OP, inventory optimization, and operational excellence methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP, APICS/CPIM/CSCP, Six Sigma, or related professional certification is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Performance Indicators&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key performance measures may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Production Plan Attainment | Capacity Utilization | Schedule Adherence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain:&lt;/strong&gt; On-Time Delivery | Material Availability | Inventory Turns | Inventory Accuracy | Logistics Cost&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EHS:&lt;/strong&gt; Safety Incident Rate | Corrective Action Closure | Regulatory Compliance | Environmental Performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Project Schedule | Project Budget | Construction Safety | Facility Readiness | Utility Reliability&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Cost Reduction | Operational Efficiency | Risk Management | Cross-Functional Execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Scope&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operations Director provides leadership and management oversight for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Planning / PMC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain &amp;amp; Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warehouse &amp;amp; Inventory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environmental, Health &amp;amp; Safety (EHS)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure / Construction / Facility Engineering &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The U.S. base salary range for this full-time position is $200,000.00 –$240,000.00, plus eligibility for 20% bonus and benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by factors such as the role, level, and geographic location. The range listed in the job posting represents the minimum and maximum target salaries for this position across all U.S. locations. Actual compensation within the range will be influenced by the specific work location, along with factors such as job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter will provide more details about the specific salary range for your preferred location during the hiring process. Please note that the listed compensation reflects the base salary only and does not include bonus or benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Gotion Inc. is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to fostering a diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve, cultivating a culture of inclusion and belonging, and ensuring equal employment opportunities for all.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We provide equal opportunity to all individuals regardless of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions (including breastfeeding), parental status, criminal histories consistent with legal requirements, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Gotion Inc., we strive to create an environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title:&lt;/strong&gt; Director of Quality&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Status:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office Hours:&lt;/strong&gt; Monday - Friday; hybrid schedule&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Boston, Massachusetts&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; $150,000 - $185,000, plus equity options. (Compensation dependent on experience level)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Quality owns Ketryx&#39;s Quality Management System (QMS), Information Security Management System (ISMS), AI governance program, and certification portfolio. This leader keeps our processes effective, scalable, and audit-ready while helping the business ship and serve enterprise customers efficiently. Because Ketryx builds compliance software for regulated industries, the role is also an internal reference user of our platform and a public voice on quality and regulatory practice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the QMS and support the ISMS:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep policies, SOPs, and records aligned with how we operate, including ISO/IEC 27001 and SOC 2 programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead AI governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Own AI policies and ISO/IEC 42001 conformity, and set assurance expectations for validated AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run audits and certifications:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead readiness and execution for ISO 13485, IEC 62304, ISO 14971, ISO/IEC 27001, SOC 2, IEC 61508, and ISO 26262, plus customer audits and supplier assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Govern change and release:&lt;/strong&gt; Define risk-based gates and evidence expectations, and own release-level risk assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable customers and deals:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain validation packages and the trust center, and support questionnaires, RFPs, and strategic accounts where compliance is a blocker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track regulation:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor emerging requirements (e.g., EU MDR, EU Cyber Resilience Act, 21 CFR Part 11) and translate them into internal and customer guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the QA/RA consulting team:&lt;/strong&gt; Staff engagements, set deliverable standards, provide final review, and develop consultants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across the company:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Engineering, Product, Security, Sales, and leadership, and represent Ketryx externally through content, conferences, and standards work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Success Is Measured&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zero major nonconformities in certification audits, with findings closed on time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All committed certifications achieved or maintained, including ISO 26262 by August 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validation packages and risk assessments published for every platform release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast, reliable responses to customer compliance inquiries and deal blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-quality consulting deliverables with zero quality-related escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years of experience in quality&lt;/strong&gt; at a MedTech, BioPharma, or Life Sciences company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record operating or leading a QMS and supporting external audits in a regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or materially supporting an ISMS under ISO/IEC 27001 or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of risk-based quality practices and change and release governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator with technical and non-technical audiences, with strong documentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on audit experience across ISO 13485, IEC 62304, ISO 14971, ISO/IEC 42001, IEC 61508, ISO 26262, and SOC 2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI governance and validating AI-enabled features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background supporting customer validation and security questionnaires for enterprise SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with functional safety tool qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team of quality or regulatory professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;What We Offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous stock options possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in an exciting field with a positive impact on the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to learn and grow as part of a global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO for full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ketryx is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, medical condition, national origin, physical or mental disability, political affiliation, protected veteran status, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ketryx&lt;/strong&gt; is saving and improving lives by making medical software safe and reliable. We empower software teams building medical applications to create safe, secure, and compliant products used by patients and providers worldwide. We believe that, by automating much of the documentation and quality processes, teams will be able to produce safer and more innovative medical software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ketryx is at the forefront of helping teams incorporate AI/ML into medical software and that’s why we need you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is a leading biotechnology company dedicated to creating and delivering the next generation of gene editing therapies to patients. The Company is leveraging its proprietary Prime Editing platform, a versatile, precise and efficient gene editing technology, to develop a new class of differentiated, one-time, potentially curative genetic therapies. Designed to make only the right edit at the right position within a gene while minimizing unwanted DNA modifications, Prime Editors have the potential to repair almost all types of genetic mutations and work in many different tissues, organs and cell types. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is currently progressing a diversified portfolio of investigational therapeutic programs organized around our core areas of focus: hematology, immunology &amp;amp; oncology, liver and lung. Across each core area, Prime Medicine is focused initially on a set of high value programs, each targeting a disease with well-understood biology and a clearly defined clinical development and regulatory path, and each expected to provide the foundation for expansion into additional opportunities. For more information, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.primemedicine.com/&quot;&gt;www.primemedicine.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is a clinical-stage biotechnology company creating the next generation of gene editing therapies. Our Prime Editing platform is versatile, precise, and efficient, with the potential to address more than 90% of known disease-causing genetic mutations. We have three programs in the clinic: an ex vivo cell therapy for an ultra-rare disease advancing toward a Biologics License Application (BLA), and two in vivo liver-targeting LNP Prime Editor programs, with more in development. We are a mission-driven team working in a lean, fast-moving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the Chief Technology Officer, the Executive Director of Supply Chain and External Manufacturing is a member of the Technology, Development and Operations (TDO) leadership team. You will own Prime Medicine’s end-to-end supply chain, from raw materials through clinical supply and commercialization, with direct accountability for materials management and for supporting internal planning and manufacturing needs. You will manage our external manufacturing partners, lead a highly functional lean team, and serve as the primary partner to Finance for TDO external spend. We are looking for a leader who embraces AI as a core part of how supply chain and external manufacturing run at Prime Medicine, from forecasting and materials visibility to partner performance and cost modeling. This role is for someone who thrives in ambiguity, is energized by building, and pairs strategic thinking with hands-on execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with the CTO and TDO leadership to define manufacturing and supply chain strategy, including network design, make-vs-buy decisions, and partner selection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-enabled operations. &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the use of AI and digital tools across supply chain and external manufacturing, including demand forecasting, materials and inventory visibility, partner performance monitoring, contract and cost modeling, and logistics tracking, as well as keeping the function ahead of new tools as they emerge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Materials management. &lt;/strong&gt;Own materials management across the portfolio, including forecasting, sourcing, purchasing, and inventory of raw materials, critical starting materials, and components, so materials are available on time for each program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning and supply operations. &lt;/strong&gt;Support internal planning and the manufacturing needs of each program; deliver labeling, packaging, shipping, and cell therapy logistics on time and in full; and resolve supply risks before they affect timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External manufacturing and partners. &lt;/strong&gt;Build and manage a network of CDMOs, CROs, and critical suppliers, including contracts, governance, performance, and qualification of new partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical and commercial readiness. &lt;/strong&gt;Ensure supply chain documentation and external site readiness support IND and BLA submissions, working with CMC, Regulatory, Quality, Non-clinical Development, Clinical, and program teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Own TDO budget development for external spend, cost projections, and financial reporting in close partnership with functional leaders and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;. Lead, coach, and inspire your team of supply chain/external manufacturing professionals and indirect colleagues across TDO; foster a culture of accountability, continuous improvement, and collaborative problem-solving and goal attainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant technical discipline; advanced degree (MS, MBA, or PhD) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15–20+ years of progressive experience in supply chain, technical operations, external manufacturing, process development, or MSAT within biotech or pharma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct ownership of materials management and clinical supply for clinical-stage programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing CDMOs and CROs, including negotiating MSAs and SOWs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cell therapy and/or LNP or nucleic acid programs; experience supporting IND/CTA and BLA/MAA submissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial acumen, including ownership of operating budgets and multi-year cost projections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of implementing AI or digital tools that improved forecasting, visibility, or decision-making in supply chain or operations, and of changing how teams work as a result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change management, project management, and communication skills, with the ability to build trust with partners, Finance, and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus: lean, fast-moving biotech; ultra-rare disease or small patient population experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Why Prime Medicine&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will matter: our programs have the potential to be curative therapies for patients with no other options, and this role directly enables that. You will be part of the TDO leadership team, with direct access to the CTO and interact with other Executive leaders, and you will shape how AI is applied to supply chain and manufacturing at a company where it is a growing priority. You will have ownership from day one in building how Prime Medicine delivers for patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, veteran status, or any other classification protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Cambridge, MA | Reports to: Chief Technology Officer | TDO Leadership Team Member&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The pay range reflects the full-time base salary range we expect to pay for this role at the time of posting. Base pay will be determined based on several factors including, but not limited to, relevant experience, skills, and education. This role is eligible for an annual short-term incentive award (e.g., bonus) and an annual long-term incentive award (e.g., equity).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package with robust health, financial, and wellness benefits—including medical, dental, vision, life insurance, a 401(k) match, and equity programs—along with generous paid time off, wellness days, and company-wide recharge breaks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to employee well-being reflects our belief that when we care for our people, we strengthen our ability to put patients first and make meaningful impact together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;U.S. Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$295,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$312,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, veteran status, or any other classification protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;About&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;At&amp;nbsp;Re:Build, our mission is to ensure the next generation of important products are made, at scale, in America. We are laying the foundation for a better future for our customers, employees, and communities by revitalizing America&#39;s manufacturing base and creating meaningful jobs across the country, including in historically deindustrialized regions.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We operate an advanced, end-to-end manufacturing platform that partners with industrial companies and innovators to take products from first concept to full-scale production in critical verticals including aerospace and defense, electrification, medical, energy and environment, and robotics and automation.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The way we operate is as important as the work we do. It&#39;s guided by The&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&amp;nbsp;Way, 16 principles that shape how we collaborate with each other, partner with our customers and vendors, and contribute to the communities where we operate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;(link to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rebuildmanufacturing.com/about/rebuild-way/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Re:Build Way principles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Re:Build Composite Resources&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composite Resources, a Re:Build Manufacturing company, is an innovative, rapidly growing manufacturer of composite components and tooling located in Rock Hill, SC. Our constantly evolving portfolio of projects includes parts and assemblies for clients in the aerospace and defense industries. At Composite Resources, we embrace a culture defined by teamwork, ownership, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composite Resources is looking for a strategic, hands-on Quality leader ready to build a quality function from the ground up during a period of significant growth. You&#39;ve successfully led a facility or special process through NADCAP certification before and know what it takes to go from readiness assessment to accreditation. You&#39;re comfortable operating at the executive level — shaping strategy and reporting directly to the President — while still rolling up your sleeves to solve problems on the floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring experience in quality systems, APQP, and Lean/Six Sigma in manufacturing, ideally within composites or aerospace. You&#39;re energized by the challenge of building a quality strategy that works for both a fast-moving, high-mix prototyping operation and a higher-volume, cost-disciplined production site — with the opportunity to build your own team and establish quality as a true competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Get To Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Lead the organization&#39;s achievement of NADCAP certification at the new site — owning the roadmap, readiness assessments, gap closure, audit prep, and accreditation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Build and lead a growing Quality team to support expansion across two facilities over the next five years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Define a culture of quality and set department goals aligned with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Implement and maintain AS9100, ISO, NADCAP, and other aerospace/composites certifications, including internal, compliance, and supplier audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Architect quality strategies tailored to two environments — balancing fast-paced prototyping with cost-efficient, higher-volume production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Partner with other departments to plan, implement, and improve quality programs supporting business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Track quality metrics and turn data/trends into improvement actions with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Apply SPC, analytics, AI tools, and Lean/A3 problem-solving to drive process improvement and error prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Engage with customers on gate reviews, documentation, deviation approvals, engineering changes, and part quality concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Ensure timely completion of quality documentation (ballooned drawings, PFMEAs, control plans, capability studies, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring To The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Quality Systems, Engineering, or related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Hands-on experience successfully achieving NADCAP certification for a site or special process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;5+ years in Quality Systems, APQP, Lean/Six Sigma, and large-scale project management in manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;2+ years in a leadership role, with proven success building and developing a quality team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of AS9100 and NADCAP requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills; ability to drive change with minimal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Ability to communicate quality objectives/requirements effectively and negotiate with customers and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Willingness to work flexibly, including occasional travel between facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strongly Preferred:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Composites and aerospace manufacturing experience, including both prototype and high-volume environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Familiarity with ISO9000, ISO13485, and ITAR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Knowledge of gauging, metrology, and CMM programming/software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Experience leveraging AI and technology to improve quality efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is $116,616 – $174,924.75 per year. This range represents the Company’s good faith estimate of the base compensation for this role at the time of posting.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation will be determined based on several factors, including but not limited to relevant experience, skills, qualifications, internal equity, and geographic location. In addition to base salary, this role may be eligible for annual incentive compensation and/or long-term incentives, subject to Company plans. The Company offers a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement, paid time off, and other benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
